// §14 entry 7 -- implicit padding in a wire struct -> EXS-E0322.
//
// §5.2's own `Capitulum` example, with the explicit `reserva` field
// REMOVED:
//
//   @transitus
//   publica structura Capitulum {
//       signum:    u32:maior
//       versio:    u8
//       genus:     u8
//       reserva:   u16:maior      // explicit; implicit padding is EXS-E0322
//       longitudo: u32:maior
//   }
//
// `versio` and `genus` together are 2 bytes; without an explicit `reserva`
// field, the 2 bytes that get `signum`/`longitudo` back onto a 4-byte
// boundary are IMPLICIT padding -- exactly the uninitialized-memory
// disclosure class §5.2 states this rule closes: "`@transitus` types may
// have no implicit padding -- explicit `reserva` fields or rejection."
//
// DEFERRED: needs the @transitus layout checker, which needs the type
// checker (Stage 2). compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty;
// `exsc aedifica`, run directly against this file, exits 0 and reports
// nothing -- confirmed, not assumed.

@transitus
publica structura Capitulum {
    signum:    u32:maior
    versio:    u8
    genus:     u8
    longitudo: u32:maior
}

